                    Sebastian Erdweg, Martin Erwig, Richard F. Paige, and Eelco Visser
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.cl.2015.08.007</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.5.2.26</data>
      <data key="d9">programming languages / compiler; semantics / formal methods; software engineering</data>
      <data key="d10">internal DSLs; external DSLs; domain-specific modeling; extensible languages; language workbenches; textual/graph-based/visual languages; language design; language implementation techniques</data>
      <data key="d11">internal DSLs; external DSLs; domain-specific modeling; extensible languages; language workbenches; textual/graph-based/visual languages; language design; language implementation techniques; programming languages / compiler; semantics / formal methods; software engineering</data>
      <data key="d12">Ralf Lämmel;Lennart Augustsson;Shriram Krishnamurthi;Yannis Smaragdakis;Eelco Visser;Peter D. Mosses;Laurence Tratt;Dániel Varró;Martin Erwig;Görel Hedin;Matthew Flatt;Richard F. Paige;Friedrich Steimann;William R. Cook;Tijs van der Storm;Eric Walkingshaw;Julia Rubin;Steven Kelly;Markus Völter;Sebastian Erdweg;Hassan Chafi;Klaus Ostermann;Andrew Gill;Daco Harkes;Oleg Kiselyov;Dimitris Kolovos;Sonja Maier;Bruno C. d. S. Oliveira;Tillmann Rendel;Ulrik Pagh Schultz;Guido Wachsmuth</data>
