                        Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                    Betty H. C. Cheng and Benoit Combemale and Robert B. France and Jean-Marc Jézéquel and Bernhard Rumpe
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-319-26172-0</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.4.10.32</data>
      <data key="d9">modelling / simulation; software engineering</data>
      <data key="d10">Modelling; Domain Specific Language; Software</data>
      <data key="d11">Modelling; Domain Specific Language; Software; modelling / simulation; software engineering</data>
      <data key="d12">Ralf Lämmel;Juha-Pekka Tolvanen;Pieter J. Mosterman;Bernhard Rumpe;Colin Atkinson;Jean-Marc Jézéquel;Mark van den Brand;Oscar M. Nierstrasz;Siobhán Clarke;Gabor Karsai;Janos Sztipanovits;Betty H. C. Cheng;Benoit Combemale;Friedrich Steimann;Antonio Vallecillo;Benoit Caillaud;Ulrich Frank;Robert B. France;Tony Clark;Markus Völter;Cedric Brun;Barrett Bryant;Julien Deantoni;Thomas Degueule;Marjan Mernik;Martin Schindler;Eugene Syriani</data>
