                        Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                    Thomas Agotnes and Nils Bulling
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.4.8.21</data>
      <data key="d9">semantics / formal methods; verification / logic</data>
      <data key="d10">Strategic logic; game theory; social laws; normative systems; argumentation theory; multi-agent systems</data>
      <data key="d11">Strategic logic; game theory; social laws; normative systems; argumentation theory; multi-agent systems; semantics / formal methods; verification / logic</data>
      <data key="d12">Mehdi Dastani;Birna Van Riemsdijk;Jan M. Broersen;Andreas Herzig;Thomas Agotnes;Valentin Goranko;Nils Bulling;Louise A. Dennis;Julian Padget;Markus Brill;Catalin Dima;Max Knobbout;Marija Slavkovik;Nicolas Troquard;Paolo Turrini;Natalia Criado;Brian Logan;Bas J. G. Testerink;Beishui Liao;Nir Oren;Sascha Ossowski;Maaike Harbers;Ho-Pun Lam;Marin Lujak;Truls Pedersen;Joshua Sack;Marc Van Zee;Laurent Vercouter</data>
