                        Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                    Sergiy Bogomolov, Martin Fränzle, Kyoko Makino, and Nacim Ramdani
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">https://doi.org/10.1145/3150928.3150938</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.6.12.1</data>
      <data key="d9">artificial intelligence / robotics; semantics / formal methods; verification / logic</data>
      <data key="d10">Cyber-physical systems; hybrid systems; verification; constraint solving; verified numerical methods; planning; optimization methods</data>
      <data key="d11">Cyber-physical systems; hybrid systems; verification; constraint solving; verified numerical methods; planning; optimization methods; artificial intelligence / robotics; semantics / formal methods; verification / logic</data>
      <data key="d12">Walid Taha;Markus Neher;Sylvie Putot;Martin Brain;Stefan Ratschan;Eric Goubault;John D. Pryce;Martin Fränzle;Stavros Tripakis;Anne Remke;Erika Abraham;Michael W. Hofbaur;Louise Trave-Massuyès;Karsten Scheibler;Eva Darulova;Sergiy Bogomolov;Xin Chen;Georgios Fainekos;Pavithra Prabhakar;Julien Alexandre dit Sandretto;Roman Bartak;Mauricio Castillo-Effen;Alexandre Chapoutot;Chih-Hong Cheng;Parasara Sridhar Duggirala;Mirco Giacobbe;Kyoko Makino;Marius Mikucionis;Ned Nedialkov;Junkil Park;Nacim Ramdani;Rajarshi Ray;Zhikun She;Yuichi Tazaki;Tino Teige;Alexander Wittig</data>
