                    Richard Hull, Agnes Koschmider, Hajo A. Reijers, and William Wong
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.03152; https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-65000-5_8; https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.03628</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.6.5.1</data>
      <data key="d9">modelling / simulation; society / human-computer interaction</data>
      <data key="d10">Business Process Management; Data Analytics; Visualization</data>
      <data key="d11">Business Process Management; Data Analytics; Visualization; modelling / simulation; society / human-computer interaction</data>
      <data key="d12">Andreas Oberweis;Thomas T. Hildebrandt;Avigdor Gal;Jianwen Su;Christian Stahl;Ingo Weber;Richard Hull;Michael zur Muehlen;Marlon Dumas;Agnes Koschmider;Hajo A. Reijers;Victoria Torres;Barbara Weber;Tamara Mchedlidze;Achim D. Brucker;Alexander Paar;Minseok Song;William Wong;Banu Aysolmaz;Fernanda Baião;Artur Caetano;Soren Debois;Kathrin Figl;Jens Gulden;Alexander Herwix;Christian Janiesch;Udo Kannengiesser;Julius Köpke;Ralf Laue;Henrik Leopold;Massimo Mecella;Hamid Reza Motahari Nezhad;Jan Recker;Flávia Santoro;Tijs Slaats;Chris Snijders;Han van der Aa;Liang Zhang</data>
