                        Creative Commons BY 4.0
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                    Paolo Bientinesi, David Ham, Furong Huang, Paul H. J. Kelly, and P. (Saday) Sadayappan
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.12.3.1</data>
      <data key="d9">Computational Engineering / Finance / and Science; Machine Learning; Mathematical Software</data>
      <data key="d10">compilers; computational science; linear algebra; machine learning; numerical methods</data>
      <data key="d15">2</data>
      <data key="d11">compilers; computational science; linear algebra; machine learning; numerical methods; Computational Engineering / Finance / and Science; Machine Learning; Mathematical Software</data>
      <data key="d12">Paul H. J. Kelly;Albert Cohen;Volker Tresp;Bora Uçar;P. (Saday) Sadayappan;Paolo Bientinesi;Richard M. Veras;Lawrence Mitchell;Charisee Chiw;Jeremy Cohen;Jutho Haegeman;David Ham;Norman Rink;Sophia Vorderwuelbecke;Furong Huang;Cem Bassoy;Simon Bonér;Teodoro Collin;Thomas Koehler;Christos Psarras;Paul Springer;Edward Stow;Carsten Uphoff;Edward Valeev;Connor Ward;Muthu Manikandan Baskaran;Nadav Cohen;Edoardo Di Napoli;Rong Ge;Johnnie Gray;Vinod Grover;Katharina Kormann;Jean Kossaifi;Jiajia Li;Devin Matthews;Luke Panayi;Vivek Srikumar;Edwin Miles Stoudenmire;Qi (Rose) Yu;Pan Zhang</data>
