                    Daniel A. Keim, Tamara Munzner, Fabrice Rossi, and Michel Verleysen
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/cgf.13092/abstract; https://doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2016.2598495</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.5.3.1</data>
      <data key="d9">computer graphics / computer vision; data bases / information retrieval; soft computing / evolutionary algorithms</data>
      <data key="d10">Information visualization; machine learning</data>
      <data key="d15">1</data>
      <data key="d11">Information visualization; machine learning; computer graphics / computer vision; data bases / information retrieval; soft computing / evolutionary algorithms</data>
      <data key="d12">David S. Ebert;Thomas Ertl;Helwig Hauser;Torsten Möller;Jarke J. van Wijk;Daniel Weiskopf;Daniel A. Keim;Barbara Hammer;Samuel Kaski;John A. Lee;Fabrice Rossi;Frank-Michael Schleif;Michel Verleysen;Thomas Villmann;Bongshin Lee;Tamara Munzner;Jing Yang;William Ribarsky;Kerstin Bunte;Stephen North;Bassam Mokbel;Daniel Archambault;Ian Nabney;Jaakko Peltonen;Leishi Zhang;Francois Blayo;Miguel Á. Carreira-Perpiñán;Ignacio Díaz Blanco;Alex Endert;Stephen Ingram;Eli Parviainen;Fernando Paulovich;Michael Sedlmair;Cagatay Turkay;William Wong;Blaz Zupan</data>
