    <node id="12051">
      <data key="d0">event</data>
      <data key="d1">12051</data>
      <data key="d2">Dagstuhl Seminar</data>
      <data key="d3">Analysis of Executables: Benefits and Challenges</data>
      <data key="d4">2012-01-29</data>
      <data key="d5">2012-02-03</data>
      <data key="d6">https://www.dagstuhl.de/12051</data>
      <data key="d13">
 &lt;p&gt;The analysis of executables is concerned with extracting information
from a binary program typically, though not exclusively, with program
analysis techniques  based on abstract interpretation. 
This topic has risen to prominence due to the need to audit code, developed
by third parties for which the source is unavailable.  Moreover, compilers are themselves
a source of bugs, hence the need to scrutinise and systematically examine executables.&lt;/p&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-33125-1_10</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.2.1.100</data>
      <data key="d9">semantics / formal methods; verification /logic; programming languages / compiler; optimization / scheduling</data>
      <data key="d10">executable analysis; reverse engineering; malware detection; control ow reconstruction</data>
      <data key="d15">1; 1</data>
      <data key="d11">executable analysis; reverse engineering; malware detection; control ow reconstruction; semantics / formal methods; verification /logic; programming languages / compiler; optimization / scheduling</data>
      <data key="d12">Barton P. Miller;David Melski;Alexey Loginov;Thomas W. Reps;Christopher Vick;Gogul Balakrishnan;Roberto Giacobazzi;Alan Mycroft;Florian Martin;Jérôme Leroux;Andrew Walenstein;Arun Lakhotia;Fausto Spoto;Axel Simon;Doina Bucur;Bjorn De Sutter;Xavier Rival;Thomas Dullien;Sébastien Bardin;Edward Barrett;Sebastian Biallas;Jörg Brauer;Mihai Christodorescu;Emmanuel Fleury;Andrea Flexeder;Sean Heelan;Paul Irofti;Johannes Kinder;Andy M. King;Junghee Lim;Bogdan Mihaila;Martin Murfitt;Magnus Myreen;Michael Petter;Edward Robbins;Daniel Roelker;Andrew Ruef;Alexander Sepp;Holger Siegel;Aditya Thakur;Aymeric Vincent;Florian Zuleger</data>
