&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Klinkhammer, D., Nitsche, M., Specht, M. and Reiterer, H. 2011. Adaptive personal territories for co-located tabletop interaction in a museum setting. &lt;em&gt;In Proc. of ITS'11 &lt;/em&gt;, New York, NY, USA, Nov. 2011, 107.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Marquardt, N., Diaz-Marino, R., Boring, S. and Greenberg, S. 2011. The proximity toolkit: prototyping proxemic interactions in ubiquitous computing ecologies. &lt;em&gt;In Proc. of UIST '11&lt;/em&gt;, New York, NY, USA, 2011, 315-326.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Marquardt, N., Hinckley, K. and Greenberg, S. 2012. Cross-device interaction via micro-mobility and f-formations. &lt;em&gt;In Proc. of UIST'12&lt;/em&gt;, New York, NY, USA, Oct. 2012, 13.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Matulic, F. and Norrie, M.C. 2013. Pen and touch gestural environment for document editing on interactive tabletops. &lt;em&gt;In Proc. of ITS'1&lt;/em&gt;, New York, NY, USA, Oct. 2013, 41-50.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Pederson, T. 2012. Proximity as Key Property in the Egocentric Interaction Paradigm. http://hci.uni-konstanz.de/proxemics/wp-content/uploads/2012/10/proxemics2012_Pedersen_et_al.pdf.
