                        Creative Commons BY 3.0 Unported license
                    &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; 
 &lt;div&gt;
&lt;img alt="Copyright" src="https://www.dagstuhl.de/_Resources/Static/Packages/Dagstuhl.Site/Frontend/images/licenses/copy.png?bust=22575bbf" style="width: 1em;"/&gt;

                    Ipek Ozkaya and Philippe Kruchten and Robert Nord and Paris Avgeriou and Carolyn Seaman
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1771/paper14.pdf; https://doi.org/10.1109/SEAA51224.2020.00067; http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1771/paper15.pdf</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.6.4.110</data>
      <data key="d9">software engineering</data>
      <data key="d10">Technical debt; Software quality; Software evolution; Software decay; Software economics; Software project management</data>
      <data key="d11">Technical debt; Software quality; Software evolution; Software decay; Software economics; Software project management; software engineering</data>
      <data key="d12">Christine Hofmeister;John D. McGregor;Robert Nord;Klaus Schmid;Alfredo Goldman;Andreas Jedlitschka;Carolyn Seaman;Guilherme Horta Travassos;Paris Avgeriou;Heiko Koziolek;Forrest Shull;Damian Andrew Tamburri;Ayse Basar Bener;Areti Ampatzoglou;Francesca Arcelli Fontana;Rami Bahsoon;Frank Buschmann;Alexandros Chatzigeorgiou;Zadia Codabux;Bill Curtis;Steven D. Fraser;Johannes Holvitie;Clemente Izurieta;Sven Johann;Philippe Kruchten;Jean-Louis Letouzey;Antonio Martini;Mehdi Mirakhorli;J. David Morgenthaler;Ipek Ozkaya;Fabio Queda Bueno da Silva;Andriy Shapochka;Will Snipes;Graziela Tonin</data>
