                    Sarah Schulz, Tarek Richard Besold, Pablo Gervás, and Evelyn Gius
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d14">https://muse.jhu.edu/article/844926 N1; https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.05888</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.9.4.87</data>
      <data key="d9">artificial intelligence / robotics; multimedia; society / human-computer interaction</data>
      <data key="d10">computational creativity; storytelling; digital humanities; digital literary studies; computational narrativity</data>
      <data key="d11">computational creativity; storytelling; digital humanities; digital literary studies; computational narrativity; artificial intelligence / robotics; multimedia; society / human-computer interaction</data>
      <data key="d12">Kai-Uwe Kühnberger;Oliver Kutz;Thierry Declerck;Tarek Richard Besold;Jonas Kuhn;Sara L. Uckelman;Nils Reiter;Sarah Schulz;Leonid Berov;Amilcar Cardoso;João Miguel Cunha;Mark Finlayson;Pablo Gervás;Evelyn Gius;Marina Grishakova;Christian Guckelsberger;Christopher Hench;Carlos León;Rafael Pérez y Pérez;Enric Plaza;Manuel Portela;Dino Pozder;Hannu Toivonen;Tony Veale;Philipp Wicke;Sina Zarrieß</data>
