&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; B. E. Brodsky and B. S. Darkhovsky. Nonparametric Methods in Change-point Problems. Springer, 1993.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; John AD Aston and Claudia Kirch. Detecting and estimating changes in dependent functional data.Journal of Multivariate Analysis, 109:204–220, 2012
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Alexander Aue and Lajos Horváth. Structural breaks in time series. Journal of Time Series Analysis, 34:1–16, 2013.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Lajos Horváth and Gregory Rice. Extensions of some classical methods in change point analysis. TEST, 23:1–37, 2014.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Alexander Tartakovsky, Igor Nikiforov, and Michele Basseville. Sequential analysis: Hypothesis testing and changepoint detection. CRC Press, 2014.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Alexander Tartakovsky. Sequential Change Detection and Hypothesis Testing: General Non-iid Stochastic Models and Asymptotically Optimal Rules. CRC Press, 2019.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Idris A Eckley, Paul Fearnhead, and Rebecca Killick. Analysis of changepoint models. In David Barber, A. Taylan Cemgil, and Silvia Chiappa, editors, Bayesian Time Series Models,
chapter 10, pages 205–224. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 2011.
&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt; Samaneh Aminikhanghahi and Diane J Cook. A survey of methods for time series change point detection. Knowledge and Information Systems, 51:339–367, 2017.
