                    Jiri Matas and Vittorio Murino and Bodo Rosenhahn and Laura Leal-Taixé
                &lt;/div&gt; 
</data>
      <data key="d8">https://doi.org/10.4230/DagRep.5.2.80</data>
      <data key="d9">artificial intelligence / robotics; computer graphics / computer vision; modelling / simulation</data>
      <data key="d10">Scene Analysis; Image Understanding; Crowd Analysis; People and Object Recognition</data>
      <data key="d15">1; 1; 1; 1; 1; 1; 1; 1; 1</data>
      <data key="d11">Scene Analysis; Image Understanding; Crowd Analysis; People and Object Recognition; artificial intelligence / robotics; computer graphics / computer vision; modelling / simulation</data>
      <data key="d12">Bernt Schiele;Reinhard Klette;Ron Kimmel;Jürgen Gall;Bodo Rosenhahn;Jan-Michael Frahm;Konrad Schindler;Laura Leal-Taixé;Gabriel Brostow;Jan Dirk Wegner;Oisin Mac Aodha;Marco Cristani;Alessio Del Bue;Markus Enzweiler;Michele Fenzi;Sanja Fidler;Robert Fisher;Shaogang Gong;Abhinav Gupta;Michal Havlena;Roberto Henschel;Esther Horbert;Jörn Jachalsky;Jiri Matas;Greg Mori;Vittorio Murino;Caroline Pantofaru;Matthias Reso;Anna Rohrbach;Min Sun;Raquel Urtasun;Sebastiano Vascon;Stefan Walk;Michael Yang;Angela Yao</data>
